From 67f6dd0d37eccb8f77a7645f0e0e9fc2ea400359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:33:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] Request the standard service tier in the Gemini path
 profiles

The four Gemini 3.8 Flash high profiles (Standard, rolling summary,
rolling summary notes-off, Provider Adapter) left request.service_tier
unset, so the provider default applied. They now set it to "standard",
the literal google-genai 2.4.0 accepts for standard processing on the
Interactions API (interaction_create_params.py:93, echoed on
Interaction.service_tier). Every action and summary request carries the
field, and run_meta.json records it as requested_service_tier. The
checked-in low Provider Adapter profile is unchanged.

Snapshot tests: every request body of the four profiles, summary
requests included, carries service_tier "standard". A configured flex
or standard tier still differs from the same config without a tier only
in that field. New tests check the SDK literal, that every
google-gemini-3-8-flash-high* profile requests standard (so none can
send flex or priority), that the served tier is recorded per step, and
that a different served tier is recorded and logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
